# Golden vectors of func_80047F30 (gDrawInGameHud), the in-game HUD call sequence.
#
# Generated by running the ORIGINAL src/game/80047F30.c together with the ORIGINAL
# src/game/8001C214.c in a host harness; only the MIPS register/asm attributes were stripped
# and the drawing primitives are stubs that record their arguments. The RECT records are
# therefore already halved and colour-widened by the retail rectangle routine itself, which
# means the values below are what the PS1 would have put into the primitive packet.
#
# A CASE line carries the input state (the retail block fields), the indented lines are the
# draw calls in order. The header globals are not repeated per line: D_8009FA00 is the gate,
# D_8009FA0C the player count, D_8009FAA4 the frame stamp.
#
#   MARKER / SLOTSBAR / TARGETPASS / MARKERS  calls without arguments
#   BAR x y intensity p3 p4 p5 flag            func_80047BE8 (doubled-free screen coords)
#   RECT r g b x=.. y=.. w=.. h=.. blend=..    func_8001C214, already halved
#   TEXT ".." x y colour                       func_80049100

CASE A_mode0_60of100 frame=16 health=60 maxhealth=100 w58=65536 w5c=65536 w64=5
  MARKER
  SLOTSBAR
  BAR 15 206 0 89 88 38 0
  TARGETPASS
  MARKERS
